                <pb facs="0421" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-23T18:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. The Bolivian Government today instructed its Ministers in the four
                    neighboring countries to urge prompt acceptance of the invitation to join with
                    the Neutral Commission in the renewal of negotiations for a peaceful
                    settlement.</p>
                <p>The British and French Ministers here today received instructions to urge Bolivia
                    to accept the League formula.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
